Maria Chen: Heads up — running the node sampleapp with our latest fetch-retry wrapper + otel auto-instrumentation; when a retry happens the X-Request-Id header gets dropped on the second attempt. Logs show different request ids so correlating logs -> traces is brittle. Repro steps below.
Samir Patel: Oof. Is the retry creating a fresh Request/opts or reusing the original?
Maria Chen: It re-creates. fetchWithRetry does something like: const opts2 = { ...opts, headers: { ...opts.headers } }; new Request(url, opts2). The OTEL fetch instrumentation mutates the Headers instance at send time (adds traceparent). Our shallow copy misses it.
Ian G: Which otel lib/version?
Maria Chen: @opentelemetry/instrumentation-fetch 1.0.2, fetch-retry v0.6. Repro snippet:
```js
// pseudo
const headers = { 'X-Request-Id': idGen() }
await fetchWithRetry(url, { headers }) // first attempt ok
// fetchWithRetry reconstructs opts -> loses mutated headers
```
Talia R: That matches what I saw: instrumentation patches the actual Headers/Request objects, not plain objects. Two options: clone Request/Headers or ensure we copy the live Headers after instrumentation runs (hard).
Samir Patel: I'd prefer reusing the Request instance for retries: pass Request into fetch and call req.clone() for subsequent attempts. That preserves any runtime injection.
devex-bot: deploy-hook: telemetry-test-app v0.6.1 deployed to staging (ci/4567) :rocket:
Ian G: Example fix for Node sampleapp:
```js
const original = new Request(url, opts)
try {
  return await fetch(original)
} catch (e) {
  return await fetch(original.clone())
}
```
This keeps OTEL-added headers like traceparent on the original. Also avoids losing any runtime mutations.
Maria Chen: I'll open a PR to update the sampleapp and add an e2e that forces a retry and asserts X-Request-Id is unchanged. Will also add a small docs blurb in SDK onboarding about retry patterns + otel.
Talia R: I can add the CI e2e asserting both X-Request-Id and traceparent survive retries, and confirm logs retain the same request id across attempts.
Samir Patel: Also add a short note about redaction: do not put PII in X-Request-Id; prefer tokenized ids. Add a logging guideline line in the sampleapp README.
Maria Chen: Yup — will include the redaction guideline and a tiny code comment showing a scrubbed log line.
